cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Bio 3D Arena: a blind comparison benchmark for generative 3D models of organisms"
message: "If you use this software or the benchmark, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Arnold
    given-names: Jaret
repository-code: "https://github.com/musharna/bio3d-arena"
url: "https://bio3d-arena.fly.dev"
abstract: >-
  Bio 3D Arena evaluates generative 3D models on biological subjects rather than
  generic objects. Voters compare anonymised 3D outputs of the same organism side
  by side — four where the task can fill a quad, two otherwise — against
  CC-licensed reference photographs of the real organism, so the judgement is
  biological fidelity rather than visual appeal. A pick-best-of-four is recorded
  as three pairwise comparisons, so the statistics are pairwise either way.
  Rankings use
  Bradley-Terry with bootstrap confidence intervals, and a generator without
  enough comparisons is reported as unranked rather than given a point estimate.
  The corpus spans plants, fungi and animals across four generation paradigms:
  single-image reconstruction, text-to-3D, LLM-authored procedural geometry, and
  agentic render-critique-revise pipelines.
keywords:
  - 3d-generation
  - benchmark
  - evaluation
  - plant-phenotyping
  - computer-vision
  - bradley-terry
license: MIT
